cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as a platform, not as a result."
title: "COSMOS Test Suite: A Platform for Trying to Disprove Cosmological Hypotheses"
abstract: >-
  A research platform for testing cosmological and fundamental-physics
  hypotheses by attempting to falsify them. Provides pre-registered analysis
  plans, adversarial review stages, look-elsewhere correction, full provenance
  chains, and reproducibility packages. No scientific findings are claimed: at
  the time of this release, none of the 35 registered research questions has
  been answered, and the single implemented experiment has only ever consumed
  synthetic data.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nortaq-PlayNexus/COSMOS-TEST-SUITE"
url: "https://github.com/Nortaq-PlayNexus/COSMOS-TEST-SUITE"
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - falsification
  - large-scale structure
  - baryon acoustic oscillations
  - reproducibility
  - scientific methodology
authors:
  - family-names: PlayNexus
    alias: Nortaq-PlayNexus
references:
  - type: standard
    title: "Planck 2018 results. VI. Cosmological parameters"
    doi: "10.1051/0004-6361/201833910"
    notes: >-
      Source of the sound horizon constant used by cosmos/cosmology.py. The
      value is taken from the published result rather than recomputed; see
      that module's docstring for why.
  - type: article
    title: "DESI 2025. II. Measurements of Baryon Acoustic Oscillations"
    doi: "10.48550/arXiv.2503.14738"
    notes: >-
      The DESI DR2 BAO vectors used for the one external validation performed.
      An unresolved labelling discrepancy in a third-party mirror is recorded
      in docs/DATA_SOURCES.md.
